PHASE 13 — Owner/Teacher Dashboard Core

Goal:
Build the central Owner/Teacher dashboard.

Pages:
- /owner/dashboard
- /owner/students
- /owner/students/[id]
- /owner/parents
- /owner/parents/[id]
- /owner/payments
- /owner/onboarding
- /owner/calendar
- /owner/homework
- /owner/scenarios
- /owner/reviews
- /owner/materials
- /owner/notifications

Dashboard cards:
- Active students
- Active child learners
- Pending payments
- Pending level checks
- Upcoming lessons today
- Homework submitted
- Scenarios submitted
- Reviews pending correction
- Students low on credits
- AI weekly summaries due

Student detail should show:
- Profile
- Level
- Package balance
- Upcoming/past lessons
- Homework history
- Scenarios
- Reviews
- Practice words
- Common mistakes
- Session notes
- AI notes/summaries
- Audit history related to student

Acceptance criteria:
- Owner can manage all core entities.
- Dashboard stats are accurate.
- Student details are useful.
- No duplicate useless actions.
- Empty states are clean.

Manual test checklist:
- Open dashboard.
- Open student detail.
- Open parent detail.
- Check pending items.
- Confirm mobile responsive.

